WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:14.599
Hi, friends. Gani here. This is The Need Namer.

00:00:14.599 --> 00:00:21.198
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:21.198 --> 00:00:25.157
Hands resting on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:25.157 --> 00:00:29.116
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:29.116 --> 00:00:38.355
Underneath a big feeling, there is very often a need. The feeling is the weather on top. The need is what is underneath, asking for something.

00:00:38.355 --> 00:00:48.913
A need can be small and plain. Rest. Help. Space. Quiet. A turn. A drink of water. A friend nearby.

00:00:48.913 --> 00:01:00.791
When the need has no name, it can come out sideways — as a shout, or tears, or a body that cannot sit still.

00:01:00.791 --> 00:01:06.070
Naming the need gives it a straight road out. Let me show you the three steps.

00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:17.948
Step one: name the feeling. Say it inside, plainly. I feel frustrated. I feel left out. I feel tired all the way down.

00:01:17.948 --> 00:01:29.826
Step two: find the need under it. Ask yourself: what would actually help right now? Not forever. Right now.

00:01:29.826 --> 00:01:41.704
Frustrated might be sitting on top of help. Left out might be sitting on top of a turn, or a friend. Tired might be sitting on top of rest.

00:01:41.704 --> 00:01:52.262
Step three: ask in plain words. I need a break. I need help with this part. I need some quiet. Short words. True words.

00:01:52.262 --> 00:01:53.582
Every need on that list counts as a real need. Rest counts. Space counts. Quiet counts. You never have to earn the right to need something.

00:01:53.582 --> 00:02:05.460
Hear this clearly: naming a need is not a demand. You are not ordering anyone. You are asking — and asking is the skill.

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:17.338
Sometimes the answer will be yes. Sometimes it will be no, or not yet. A no to the ask is survivable. It is not a no to you.

00:02:17.338 --> 00:02:26.577
And naming a need is never complaining, and it is never weakness. It is one of the strongest, clearest things a person can say.

00:02:26.577 --> 00:02:27.896
Your needs are yours. They are never measured against a classmate's needs, and nobody ranks them. A need does not have to be the biggest one in the room to be real.

00:02:27.896 --> 00:02:37.135
Name the feeling. Find the need. Ask in plain words.

00:02:37.135 --> 00:02:43.734
Shoulders soft. Let your body rest.

00:02:43.734 --> 00:02:49.013
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:02:49.013 --> 00:02:55.612
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:02:55.612 --> 00:03:02.211
You're ready for what's next.
